==English==
{{wikipedia|female (disambiguation)|female}}
[[File:Venus symbol (fixed width).svg|thumb|The female symbol {{angbr|[[♀]]}}]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁(y)-}}
{{etymon|en|id=sex|inh|enm>female>sex|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|female}}, an alteration of Middle English {{m|enm|femele}}, from {{der|en|fro|femele}}, {{m|fro|femelle||female}}, from {{der|en|ML.|fēmella||a female}}, from {{der|en|la|fēmella||a girl, a young female, a young woman}}, diminutive of {{m|la|fēmina||a woman}}. The English spelling and pronunciation were remodelled under the influence of {{m|en|male}}, which is otherwise not etymologically related. Contrast {{m|en|woman}}, which ''is'' etymologically built on {{m|en|man}} (as in person).

